# Private names that must never reach a published copy of this repository.
#
# Copy this file to .private-names (git-ignored, never committed) and replace
# the entries with the names of your own projects, machines and networks.
# Then run `sh scripts/check-private-names.sh` before publishing or releasing.
#
# Format: one extended regular expression per line; blank lines and lines
# starting with # are ignored. Every pattern is matched against every tracked
# file (case-sensitive), so keep them specific enough to avoid noise.

# Project / business names, product and customer names
acme-legacy-app
some-customer-portal
Some Business System

# Personal environment: user names, machine names, worker ids
alice
my-desktop-pc
w-alice-laptop

# Internal addresses that must not be published (RFC 1918 ranges you use)
172\.20\.[0-9]
10\.12\.34\.
